# Read-only relay between webui-backend and the KMEs, public host only
# (deploy/docker-compose.cloud.yml, service kme-relay).
#
# The KMEs serve the ETSI GS QKD 014 key API, the ETSI GS QKD 004 binding,
# /internal/sync and the simulator's control routes without authentication.
# On the public host webui-backend answers the internet through Caddy, so it
# does not share a network with the KMEs. It reaches them only through this
# relay, which passes the reads the backend makes and refuses everything else:
# no key route, no KME-to-KME route and no write. The nodes still reach the key
# API on qkd-net; the backend is not on qkd-net, and this relay is its only way
# to a KME.
#
# Port 8081 is bb84-kme-a and 8082 is bb84-kme-b. The path list is the set of
# GET requests webui-backend sends to a KME, plus /health for the container's
# own health check; tests/test_the_004_binding_is_not_public.py fails if the
# backend starts reading a path that is not listed here. Paths match exactly,
# so /sim/params does not let /sim/params/reset through.
{
	admin off
	auto_https off
	persist_config off
}

:8081 {
	@read {
		method GET HEAD
		path /health /sim/stats /sim/params /sim/params/editable /sim/keyrate/crosscheck
	}
	handle @read {
		reverse_proxy bb84-kme-a:8080
	}
	handle {
		respond 403
	}
}

:8082 {
	@read {
		method GET HEAD
		path /health /sim/stats /sim/params /sim/params/editable /sim/keyrate/crosscheck
	}
	handle @read {
		reverse_proxy bb84-kme-b:8080
	}
	handle {
		respond 403
	}
}
